# Integer SPIR-V peepholes, each proved by SAT (live sessions: "SAT simplify").
# Power-of-two multiply + divide: the multiply becomes a shift (driver-trivial).
SAT simplify nofile
```spv
%a = OpIMul %uint %x %uint_8
%b = OpUDiv %uint %a %uint_2
OpStore %out %b
```
# An extract at bit 0 is a mask.
SAT simplify nofile
```spv
%a = OpBitFieldUExtract %uint %x %uint_0 %uint_8
OpStore %out %a
```
# UClamp with a low bound that can never bite becomes a min.
SAT simplify nofile
```spv
%a = OpExtInst %uint %glsl UClamp %x %uint_0 %uint_255
OpStore %out %a
```
# A select of a value and a constant: SAT keeps a min when the compare is irrelevant.
SAT simplify nofile
```spv
%j = OpULessThan %bool %x %uint_8
%k = OpSelect %uint %j %x %uint_8
OpStore %out %k
```
# Two constant shifts are one.
SAT simplify nofile
```spv
%a = OpShiftLeftLogical %uint %x %uint_1
%b = OpShiftLeftLogical %uint %a %uint_2
OpStore %out %b
```
# A shift-and-add chain folds into one multiply (proof: algebra mod 2^w).
SAT simplify nofile
```spv
%a = OpIMul %uint %x %uint_3
%b = OpIMul %uint %a %uint_5
OpStore %out %b
```
# x - x and x ^ x are each always zero.
SAT simplify nofile
```spv
%a = OpISub %uint %x %x
%b = OpBitwiseXor %uint %x %x
OpStore %out %a
OpStore %out2 %b
```
# A phi at a merge: either incoming value already fits in a byte.
SAT simplify nofile
```spv
OpSelectionMerge %m None
OpBranchConditional %c %l1 %l2
%l1 = OpLabel
%p = OpBitwiseAnd %uint %x %uint_127
OpBranch %m
%l2 = OpLabel
%q = OpShiftRightLogical %uint %y %uint_24
OpBranch %m
%m = OpLabel
%v = OpPhi %uint %p %l1 %q %l2
%w = OpExtInst %uint %glsl UMin %v %uint_255
OpStore %out %w
```
# Division by zero is undefined for every input: the whole value is vacuously 0.
SAT simplify nofile
```spv
%a = OpSDiv %int %sx %int_0
OpStore %out %a
```
# A constant above 2^32 folds modulo the operand width.
SAT simplify nofile
```spv
%a = OpIAdd %uint %x %uint_4294967296
OpStore %out %a
```
# An assumption on a shift amount enables the merge that is otherwise rejected.
SAT simplify n in [1, 31) nofile
```spv
%a = OpShiftLeftLogical %uint %x %uint_1
%b = OpShiftLeftLogical %uint %a %n
OpStore %out %b
```
